#: 1a5a9b82181347928baf47fd24b4496a
msgid "Daniele's guide to translation: Sphinx, RTD, Github, Transifex"
msgstr ""

#: c0e3a896b69b44139c438a5c2c5a2201
msgid "This is a pretty standard workflow for Sphinx documentation:"
msgstr ""

#: ab62a2f714294c1289008d42bfbb1bb1
msgid ""
"You maintain your documentation source in Git, on GitHub. It's published on "
"Read the Docs. Translations are managed on Transifex."
msgstr ""

#: bd11a8d2299b48519d0b2b463d003dcf
msgid ""
"All three platforms - GitHub, RTD and Transifex - play nicely together so "
"that changes to the project's content are automatically sent for translation"
" to Transifex, and get themselves published, all with minimal work for you "
"the maintainer."
msgstr ""

#: e1a60fffdc074e069a3bf3bd07a922c6
msgid "Basic translation workflow"
msgstr ""

#: a7979c70c6ff449aa87491696895244d
msgid "The very basic translation workflow is:"
msgstr ""

#: 823fffec85aa4be89e86367c25dbae22
msgid ""
"generate a ``.pot`` file (\"Portable Object Template\" – essentially, "
"translation source files)  for each of the pages of your documentation"
msgstr ""

#: a39b7a37f08c450bbb46036726d2dc0f
msgid "generate/update corresponding ``.po`` files for each target language"
msgstr ""

#: f253050a66a84c8aaa16070d2842ae84
msgid "edit the ``.po`` files to add/update the translations"
msgstr ""

#: 7be051a1c60746b28bcbd42f05f405f5
msgid "build the translated documentation from the ``.po`` files"
msgstr ""

#: 60c3f49764874dcbbecf8acb39c45c21
msgid ""
"When using Transifex, instead of editing ``.po`` files locally, the source "
"strings in the ``.pot`` files are sent to Transifex, translated there, and "
"then the translated strings pulled back down into ``.po`` files."
msgstr ""

#: 39d31042aaee420da2e33aa7b57e8faf
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: f6fe46de11d141c2aa32e485528afc77
msgid "You need to have your project up and running, and published on RTD."
msgstr ""

#: 9bcc1dee430348398be2563e221da569
msgid "Edit ``conf.py``::"
msgstr ""

#: ebfa055d65e149c2bb83a6ca17296197
msgid ""
"We need a ``transifex.yaml`` file in the repository, so Transifex knows how "
"to behave::"
msgstr ""

#: 62bce908cdd14ccb880e8d1fa7196227
msgid "Executing the workflow"
msgstr ""

#: dc45f73dec97460d887505fcd7326bad
msgid ""
"Generate the ``.pot`` files Run: ``make gettext``. This will create a "
"``gettext`` directory inside your build directory (usually, ``_build``) "
"containing a ``.pot`` file for each page."
msgstr ""

#: 6cc5fb1422d4423a9acfd1bf5bf8480a
msgid ""
"``_build`` is excluded from commits, but the ``.pot`` files need to be "
"committed, so use ``make copy-pot-files`` to copy them to ``.pot`` files in "
"``translation/source``."
msgstr ""

#: 67e1c35bf15f4639ad3fe52ac6ccd9ec
msgid "Then the changes can be committed and pushed."
msgstr ""

#: 9e4893cebd524e49a4b54a016f111789
msgid ""
"The next thing is to get the ``.pot`` files into Transifex. Transifex should"
" do that itself, watching GitHub for changes."
msgstr ""
